WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.200
When we last saw Dexter Morgan, he had abandoned&nbsp;
his young son, faked his death, and become,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.320
well, a lumberjack — complete with a big beard&nbsp;
and his own small trailer in the middle of Oregon.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:15.280
The new revival of the popular Dexter series&nbsp;
on Showtime, set eight years after the finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.360
will see the well-meaning titular serial&nbsp;
killer, played by Michael C. Hall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.880
living under an assumed identity in Iron Lake, New&nbsp;
York. He'll be dealing with new setbacks and foes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:30.480
including the villainous Mayor Caldwell, played by&nbsp;
Clancy Brown, and Chief of Police Angela Bishop,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:36.080
played by Julia Jones. As executive producer&nbsp;
Clyde Phillips warned viewers, heads will roll.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.640
"This is Dexter. People are going to die."

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.600
When John Lithgow was added to the revival,&nbsp;
however, fans were understandably curious about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.560
what his actual role would be; his character,&nbsp;
Arthur Mitchell, AKA the Trinity Killer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.520
was killed by Dexter at the end of Season 4.&nbsp;
How exactly does someone come back from that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.480
especially with Dexter's patented methods&nbsp;
that assure his victims are truly gone?

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.680
John Lithgow won an Emmy for his&nbsp;
frightening work as Mitchell and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.920
was arguably a pivotal character on the&nbsp;
show. He was a foil for Dexter who could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:10.880
seemingly balance his double life as a serial&nbsp;
killer with his role as a husband and father.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.880
In some ways, Dexter finally found&nbsp;
someone he could relate to as a person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:20.240
at least when it came to his most primal desires&nbsp;
and the justifications of his actions. By killing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:25.360
Dexter's wife Rita, however, the Trinity Killer —&nbsp;
a man who was abusive toward his own family — put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:30.400
an end to Dexter's dream of "having it all" as&nbsp;
both a killer and a family man. Dexter kills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.440
Mitchell and the Trinity Killer persona along with&nbsp;
him, though his inner peace is still years away.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.840
We can speculate about how Arthur will return&nbsp;
to the show, but according to Deadline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:45.280
Lithgow is only working for about a day on set. If&nbsp;
this is the case, it's unlikely that his character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.560
will be a consistent presence during the revival.&nbsp;
We also don't expect him to portray someone other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.760
than Mitchell, as the Trinity Killer is still one&nbsp;
of the most unsettling characters in all of TV.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:59.040
There must be a specific reason&nbsp;
that Lithgow has rejoined the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.640
and for this, we need to look deeply&nbsp;
into the personality of Dexter.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.120
How long can Dexter suppress his natural urges?&nbsp;
That should be one of the biggest questions you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:11.600
ask when the new episodes air. Away from the&nbsp;
constant threat and temptation that a "normal"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:16.640
life brought him, Dexter's new weapon of choice is&nbsp;
an axe. But instead of cutting into human flesh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.240
he's cutting into trees. It can't&nbsp;
possibly be what he really wants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.640
could it? Somewhere inside, an inner voice&nbsp;
pokes at him, reminding him of his true nature.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.040
"Hello … Dexter Morgan"

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.600
While Dexter may have decided toward the end of&nbsp;
his run as a killer that he no longer needs the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:40.400
Code, that doesn't mean his demons have left.&nbsp;
The Trinity Killer took Dexter's wife away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.840
cutting deeper than any blade. It's&nbsp;
not much of a stretch to think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.840
the Dark Passenger could return. But&nbsp;
this time, what if it bears a new face?

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.640
A simple reminder of who Dexter is and what&nbsp;
he's capable of wouldn't take much dialogue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.880
Lithgow probably didn't need more than a day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.800
on set to deliver an emotionally&nbsp;
compelling exchange with Dexter.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.560
Their scene, or scenes, could be the&nbsp;
catalyst that causes Dexter to return to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:07.520
his murderous life. Or it might be a final&nbsp;
catharsis for the former forensics master.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.920
Although The Trinity Killer is back, that doesn't&nbsp;
mean Dexter will snap and murder the first person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.480
who he thinks deserves it. Let's be honest,&nbsp;
though: What is Dexter without a high body count?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.800
Viewers aren't going to return for the reformed&nbsp;
killer who has conquered his emotional and mental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.120
instabilities. Closure for the audience&nbsp;
may not be the same as closure for Dexter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:30.400
and we won't be surprised if Arthur Mitchell is&nbsp;
the spark that lights a new fire in Dexter's soul.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.720
We'll find out exactly how Arthur Mitchell will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:37.120
return to Dexter when the revival&nbsp;
premieres in the fall of 2021.

